WEBVTT

00:02.093 --> 00:05.977
[It is better to suffer an
injustice than to commit one.]

00:05.978 --> 00:12.012
[It is better to suffer an
injustice than to commit one.]
[Cicero, Tusculan Disputations]

00:12.905 --> 00:16.158
I have the results of your latest exams.

00:21.194 --> 00:23.003
You all passed.

00:23.191 --> 00:25.776
- Yes!
- That means we're moving up!

00:25.801 --> 00:28.278
- Seriously?!
- This is great!

00:28.451 --> 00:32.130
This is the most satisfactory
work I've ever seen from you.

00:32.482 --> 00:34.982
The test was just too easy!

00:35.007 --> 00:37.385
Says the guy with the second-lowest score.

00:37.425 --> 00:40.165
Yours was the lowest. You have no room to talk.

00:40.190 --> 00:42.119
Hey, where do you get off?!

00:42.491 --> 00:45.010
- What an idiot.
- Takes one to know one!

00:45.069 --> 00:46.924
That makes you both idiots.

00:46.949 --> 00:48.423
However…

00:49.054 --> 00:54.366
we've reached the end of finals,
and no one has been expelled.

00:55.090 --> 00:58.918
This has never happened in school history.

01:00.109 --> 01:04.940
Accordingly, an additional
special exam is to be held.

01:05.714 --> 01:06.886
What do you mean?

01:06.911 --> 01:07.784
But why?

01:07.843 --> 01:09.152
No one told us.

01:09.177 --> 01:11.536
- That's way too much!
- What gives?!

01:11.561 --> 01:13.634
Why is this happening?

01:13.933 --> 01:17.202
The administration acknowledges
your excellent achievement.

01:17.332 --> 01:18.698
So what's the problem?

01:18.723 --> 01:19.988
Yeah, tell us why!

01:20.013 --> 01:26.629
The other homeroom teachers and I also understand
that this is an unexpected burden for you.

01:27.528 --> 01:32.196
Meaning Chabashira isn't happy with
how the school is handling this, either.

01:32.860 --> 01:35.106
However, you have no grounds to refuse.

01:35.478 --> 01:38.680
Ma'am, what kind of exam will it be?

01:38.837 --> 01:41.083
The special exam is to be…

01:41.942 --> 01:43.661
a class poll.

03:16.981 --> 03:20.379
Allow me to explain the rules
of the class poll exam.

03:20.868 --> 03:27.371
In four days, you will evaluate your classmates,
and vote for the three most deserving of praise,

03:27.762 --> 03:32.644
and three deserving of criticism.

03:33.676 --> 03:38.266
The student with the most positive
votes will receive a new benefit

03:38.461 --> 03:42.269
known as a protection point.

03:42.637 --> 03:44.336
Protection point?

03:44.516 --> 03:49.271
If that student is ever to be expelled,
this will allow them to reverse the decision.

03:49.395 --> 03:50.332
Seriously?!

03:50.371 --> 03:52.371
- Whoa!
- That rules!

03:52.438 --> 03:53.414
Best reward ever!

03:53.438 --> 03:56.610
They pulled out all the stops
with the reward this time.

03:57.138 --> 04:00.868
Is there some penalty for the students
with the most negative votes?

04:01.123 --> 04:03.739
Only the one lowest scoring student.

04:03.896 --> 04:09.743
The goal of this exam is to determine
the top and bottom student

04:09.767 --> 04:14.296
by calculating all positive and negative votes.

04:14.677 --> 04:16.548
The lowest scoring student?

04:17.802 --> 04:23.114
Why would the school offer a reward
as exceptional as a protection point?

04:23.388 --> 04:29.950
Only to balance an exam that likely cannot
be completed without any expulsions.

04:30.791 --> 04:34.521
That's right. The student with
the most negative votes

04:35.224 --> 04:37.802
will be expelled from the school.

04:40.552 --> 04:42.240
- Huh?!
- You gotta be kidding!

04:42.291 --> 04:44.291
- No way…
- But we just passed.

04:44.439 --> 04:45.243
Moreover,

04:45.474 --> 04:51.821
the protection point the top student wins
cannot be transferred to another student.

04:52.130 --> 04:55.646
That means someone will
be expelled no matter what.

04:56.954 --> 05:01.407
It's simple, yet still the most brutal exam yet.

05:01.698 --> 05:03.630
Wait, this makes no sense!

05:03.655 --> 05:06.640
You're saying someone gets
kicked out no matter what?

05:06.776 --> 05:12.963
Correct. However, there will be no penalty
to the class for this particular expulsion.

05:12.963 --> 05:16.248
Isn't someone getting expelled already a penalty?

05:16.557 --> 05:19.369
The protection point is an abnormally high reward.

05:20.151 --> 05:25.932
But even so, the risk we face
to earn it is disproportionate.

05:26.557 --> 05:29.287
It's only natural that you find it unreasonable.

05:29.503 --> 05:35.537
But now that the rules are in place, you have
no choice but to tackle the exam accordingly.

05:35.811 --> 05:37.921
That's life in human society.

05:38.546 --> 05:45.166
Sakayanagi's father is chairman. He doesn't seem
like the type to hold such an absurd exam.

05:45.538 --> 05:47.423
Let's not lose hope yet.

05:47.448 --> 05:49.813
We've always found our way through so far.

05:49.838 --> 05:52.754
There must be a way to for everyone to pass again.

05:53.038 --> 06:00.576
Hirata is right. For instance, we could organize
our votes so that everyone gets the same total.

06:00.889 --> 06:03.213
No, I'm afraid that's futile.

06:03.331 --> 06:08.936
Voting will be repeated until someone
is selected to be expelled.

06:09.756 --> 06:14.912
In addition, one positive vote from the students
outside our class will also be added.

06:15.382 --> 06:19.879
This makes it impossible to control
the outcome from within the class.

06:20.186 --> 06:24.053
Ma'am, didn't you say it "likely"
can't be done without an expulsion?

06:24.092 --> 06:28.037
Well, it's a different story
if you use private points.

06:28.428 --> 06:34.229
For a payment of 200,000 private points,
the school won't refuse to overturn an expulsion.

06:34.542 --> 06:36.542
200,000 points…

06:36.788 --> 06:40.479
We can't afford to spend that much
just to save one person.

06:40.557 --> 06:43.975
So by the end of this, someone
in this class is gonna…

06:44.151 --> 06:47.358
Ugh, what the hell are we supposed to do?

06:47.382 --> 06:48.819
- This is the worst exam ever!

06:48.819 --> 06:50.342
- Be quiet, Yamauchi!
- This is the worst exam ever!

06:50.378 --> 06:54.289
Why should I? I bet you're planning
to vote against me, aren't you?!

06:54.362 --> 06:56.725
No one's gonna say who they're voting for.

06:56.750 --> 07:01.490
See, I knew it! I'll vote against you,
too, and see how you like it!

07:01.546 --> 07:02.988
How uncouth.

07:03.013 --> 07:03.548
What?

07:03.698 --> 07:08.385
This exam will affect us for the next two years.

07:08.639 --> 07:11.530
I wouldn't get too comfortable if I were you!

07:11.803 --> 07:15.651
You just don't get it, do you, Redhead?

07:15.710 --> 07:16.311
Huh?!

07:16.550 --> 07:23.131
There is no penalty to the class, so isn't this
just a chance to delete a classmate we don't need?

07:23.444 --> 07:26.881
Like one of those incompetent friends of yours.

07:27.018 --> 07:28.823
- Incompetent?
- Hey, watch it!

07:28.874 --> 07:31.326
Settle down. Let's think about this calmly.

07:31.413 --> 07:35.944
Easy for you to say, Hirata. There's no way
you'd get the most negative votes.

07:36.569 --> 07:39.108
Aren't you the safest one of all?

07:39.146 --> 07:41.336
I don't know how it'll turn out for me.

07:41.510 --> 07:44.362
Oh, you don't know, huh?

07:44.387 --> 07:46.764
Of course you do. If anyone's safe, its you.

07:46.764 --> 07:48.912
Must be nice to be popular.

07:48.952 --> 07:51.346
- You're never getting expelled.
- Hirata…

07:51.491 --> 07:55.084
Yeah, stay out of it!
We're talking to Kouenji right now.

07:55.109 --> 07:56.851
That's enough, Sudou.

07:57.000 --> 07:58.347
Suzune…

07:58.445 --> 08:03.210
There's plenty of time before we have to vote.
Let's think this through as a group.

08:03.504 --> 08:07.937
This may go without saying, but you cannot
abstain, nor vote anonymously.

08:08.445 --> 08:13.618
You may not vote for yourself, either,
or for the same person more than once.

08:14.379 --> 08:20.179
I'm sure you'll find this troubling, but
the school has designated these rules.

08:20.922 --> 08:24.594
As long as you're at this school,
you must follow its rules.

08:25.121 --> 08:27.855
Voting will be held in four days.

08:28.597 --> 08:29.593
Any questions?

08:33.148 --> 08:36.515
Ugh, isn't this like, the actual worst?

08:36.625 --> 08:39.183
Do you think there's some kind of trick to it?

08:39.476 --> 08:42.171
All we can do is coordinate our votes.

08:42.308 --> 08:47.015
This is just an idea, but
what if we vote as a group?

08:47.406 --> 08:50.374
Like, give our positive votes to each other?

08:50.648 --> 08:56.858
Right. None of us would get the reward,
but we could all stay out of the bottom spot.

08:57.035 --> 09:02.210
Can we do that, though? Ms. Chabashira said
we can't control this from within our class.

09:02.289 --> 09:06.253
I'm sure some people will group up
to stay safe, even if we don't.

09:06.605 --> 09:10.276
I'm in favor of grouping up
to protect each other, too.

09:10.725 --> 09:13.441
I don't want to lose anyone here.

09:13.768 --> 09:15.291
M-Me neither!

09:15.305 --> 09:16.854
That's settled, then.

09:17.382 --> 09:21.131
I'll get ahead of the game and talk to the others.

09:21.186 --> 09:25.506
No, we'd better not risk provoking
anyone before the exam.

09:25.878 --> 09:28.084
You mean, so no one targets us?

09:28.193 --> 09:29.879
Yeah. The way this exam works…

09:29.879 --> 09:34.373
Any student low enough on the pecking order

09:34.452 --> 09:37.557
is an easy target for negative votes.

09:40.790 --> 09:43.524
I should strike while I can, too.

09:44.042 --> 09:48.990
[Classroom of the Elite
3rd Season]

09:58.544 --> 10:01.512
He certainly seems at ease.

10:01.844 --> 10:03.172
Horikita.

10:06.669 --> 10:08.895
Carefree, aren't you, Ryuuen?

10:11.337 --> 10:14.813
Well, if it isn't Suzune.

10:14.989 --> 10:16.145
And…

10:16.169 --> 10:18.481
you've got your little sidekick with you.

10:21.316 --> 10:24.421
Well? Did you need something?

10:24.832 --> 10:28.962
How do you plan to approach the upcoming exam?

10:29.265 --> 10:31.276
I'm not planning anything.

10:31.820 --> 10:35.062
You're prepared to be expelled
with no complaints, then.

10:35.414 --> 10:36.819
We'll see.

10:37.211 --> 10:41.800
I'm sure there are plenty of people
who would be happy to see you go.

10:42.289 --> 10:45.687
Regardless of the outcome, you went too far.

10:45.770 --> 10:48.519
There's no one left who'd be willing to save you.

10:48.523 --> 10:54.339
As an enemy, getting rid of me
now is your best bet.

10:54.711 --> 10:58.241
Class D won't stand a chance
against you with me gone.

10:58.266 --> 11:00.493
You still think so highly of yourself.

11:00.726 --> 11:06.273
Didn't you end up in Class D in the first place
because you fell short as a leader?

11:06.488 --> 11:07.816
You've got me there.

11:08.129 --> 11:13.148
This may be the last time we speak,
so would you answer something for me?

11:13.675 --> 11:16.839
You're worse off going into this exam than anyone.

11:16.937 --> 11:22.581
If you did everything you could, is there any way
you could make it through without being expelled?

11:23.793 --> 11:26.898
What a stupid question. Of course I could.

11:27.270 --> 11:29.632
You can still bluff with the best of them.

11:29.647 --> 11:35.784
Is that all? Or do you want me to hold your hand
and walk you through the solution, too?

11:35.809 --> 11:36.760
No need.

11:36.905 --> 11:40.667
I may be playing right into your hands
if I let you keep talking.

11:41.175 --> 11:45.788
Still, thank you.
Now that I see you're facing reality,

11:46.234 --> 11:49.066
I feel a little more confident in my decision.

11:49.292 --> 11:50.745
What decision?

11:50.980 --> 11:57.132
If an expulsion is inevitable, all that's left
is to simply choose the most suitable target.

11:57.425 --> 12:01.878
That approach might just backfire on you.

12:02.113 --> 12:06.155
If it does, I suppose it's only
proof that I wasn't good enough.

12:06.175 --> 12:08.382
Putting on a brave front, are we?

12:09.812 --> 12:13.816
It's not easy to just get rid of someone.

12:15.023 --> 12:20.999
It is for me. Since my first day here, I've had
no sympathy for anyone who holds us back.

12:21.332 --> 12:22.581
No, you're bluffing.

12:22.640 --> 12:24.300
How would you know?

12:24.632 --> 12:26.956
I know you inside and out.

12:27.038 --> 12:31.644
I can see your tells every time
you open your pretty little mouth.

12:32.421 --> 12:37.737
You don't even have the guts
to face your own brother.

12:38.226 --> 12:42.845
You're still floundering in the end, aren't you?

12:43.539 --> 12:45.476
And, besides…

12:45.761 --> 12:49.710
you've gotten way too comfortable
in that class of yours.

12:49.964 --> 12:53.870
You won't be able to keep your head for long.

12:54.357 --> 13:01.017
The only ones who can are people like me or
Sakayanagi, who sees her classmates as mere pawns.

13:01.527 --> 13:05.745
You can talk tough, but you don't
even have a plan, do you?

13:06.468 --> 13:08.468
What makes you so sure?

13:08.714 --> 13:12.093
Because you're going to be expelled.

13:12.230 --> 13:15.198
I'll be a big boy and take what comes to me.

13:19.574 --> 13:23.261
Don't you go wasting chances, now.

13:24.417 --> 13:30.999
I don't think I want Ryuuen to be expelled.

13:31.254 --> 13:33.021
He's always posturing.

13:33.402 --> 13:37.816
He can fight it all he wants,
and he'll still end up expelled.

13:37.953 --> 13:39.398
I'm not so sure.

13:39.554 --> 13:42.562
He might actually have some kind of plan.

13:42.797 --> 13:47.855
It's too late for him to avoid negative votes
even if he shapes up and plays nice now.

13:48.031 --> 13:51.331
Yeah. He has no straightforward way to win.

13:51.410 --> 13:53.616
So that's all there is to it.

13:54.183 --> 13:56.898
He had a point about one thing, though.

13:57.200 --> 13:58.553
And what would that be?

13:58.734 --> 14:02.550
Don't you think you should try
talking to your brother

14:02.836 --> 14:05.999
at least once before he graduates?

14:06.195 --> 14:09.359
He wouldn't humor me even if I tried.

14:09.613 --> 14:14.788
I hate to say it, but the only one
he has any regard for is you.

14:16.019 --> 14:18.558
Well, you may be right.

14:19.125 --> 14:20.882
I don't like your tone.

14:24.379 --> 14:27.952
She still has such a complex about him.

14:32.875 --> 14:34.007
What is it?

14:34.320 --> 14:38.773
So, hey. What am I, like,
supposed to do for this exam?

14:39.398 --> 14:43.050
Isn't anyone in your inner circle grouping up?

14:43.363 --> 14:45.081
Some of them, sure.

14:45.762 --> 14:48.285
Everyone's afraid of getting expelled.

14:48.762 --> 14:52.972
Honestly, like, I think there are
some people who don't like me.

14:53.050 --> 14:56.429
I wouldn't be surprised if you
got some negative votes.

14:56.479 --> 15:00.452
Hey! You're supposed to lie
and say everyone loves me!

15:00.941 --> 15:03.968
Just try to be on your best behavior for now.

15:04.320 --> 15:07.835
Got it. I'll try not to start anything.

15:08.129 --> 15:13.909
It might actually work in your favor
that you broke up with Hirata.

15:13.968 --> 15:14.671
Huh?

15:14.696 --> 15:17.837
If you were with the guy all the girls like,

15:18.042 --> 15:23.490
maybe they'd try to get
you expelled to split you up.

15:23.548 --> 15:25.413
Wow, yikes.

15:25.424 --> 15:26.968
You might be right, though.

15:27.269 --> 15:31.973
You should be fine. You just kind of
blend in, and get average grades.

15:32.172 --> 15:35.414
Who are you gonna give your bad votes to?

15:35.531 --> 15:40.042
Whoever won't benefit the class going forward.

15:40.375 --> 15:44.534
Jeez, you're cold as ice.
That figures for you, though.

15:44.808 --> 15:47.894
I have to be, if someone has to get expelled.

15:48.070 --> 15:51.370
Hey, wait, you're not talking about me, right?

15:51.468 --> 15:56.273
You're an important part of the class.
I wouldn't do that.

15:56.547 --> 15:59.399
O-Oh. Thought so.

15:59.457 --> 16:04.866
If you form a group, you can influence the voting
on grounds other than just grades.

16:04.922 --> 16:06.038
For real?

16:06.215 --> 16:11.113
Let me know if you find out about anyone
in our class trying to guide the negative votes.

16:11.138 --> 16:14.749
Okay, I'll get back to you soon. Later.

16:14.808 --> 16:15.804
Bye.

16:26.683 --> 16:28.683
He's late.

16:28.793 --> 16:32.425
I suppose waiting here was a bad idea.

16:32.894 --> 16:34.398
But…

16:36.332 --> 16:38.332
I've been expecting you.

16:39.457 --> 16:41.191
Good morning, Ayanokouji.

16:41.620 --> 16:42.737
I'm going to class.

16:42.797 --> 16:44.251
Yeah, I'll be there soon.

16:46.097 --> 16:47.972
Good morning!

16:47.997 --> 16:50.434
Oh, morning, Ichinose.

16:50.884 --> 16:52.884
So, um…

16:53.599 --> 16:55.010
It sure is cold out, huh!

16:55.239 --> 16:56.606
I guess so.

16:57.020 --> 17:00.473
Are you walking to school with someone today?

17:00.519 --> 17:01.821
Nope.

17:02.017 --> 17:05.473
Then, um… can I walk with you?

17:05.884 --> 17:06.996
Sure.

17:09.829 --> 17:14.262
This exam must be tricky for Class B.

17:14.344 --> 17:17.445
Oh, yeah. It really is.

17:17.494 --> 17:20.766
I think it's the hardest one for us yet.

17:20.772 --> 17:21.920
I figured.

17:22.231 --> 17:24.925
But we just have to do what we can, right?

17:25.102 --> 17:27.875
Don't tell me you're giving up.

17:28.148 --> 17:30.668
Huh?! No way…

17:31.059 --> 17:33.344
That's not what I'm saying at all.

17:34.145 --> 17:38.852
Just so you know, no one's
gonna be voting against you.

17:38.911 --> 17:42.016
I never said I thought I'd be expelled.

17:42.041 --> 17:43.829
It's written all over your face.

17:43.854 --> 17:46.094
What?! R-Really?

17:46.212 --> 17:48.649
I'm serious, they'd never vote against you.

17:48.862 --> 17:53.028
Oh… I suppose you're right…

17:53.341 --> 17:55.938
Are you sacrificing yourself for someone?

17:56.036 --> 17:58.789
Well… not really, no.

17:59.376 --> 18:03.555
I just think I have to take on
the risk myself, and fight this.

18:05.294 --> 18:07.633
Let's not go into too much detail, though!

18:07.735 --> 18:09.879
We're in different classes, after all.

18:10.059 --> 18:11.309
Yeah, true.

18:11.579 --> 18:13.668
Are you going to be okay?

18:14.000 --> 18:16.600
Hm… I guess we'll see.

18:17.048 --> 18:22.789
Should I put in a positive vote
for you from my class?

18:23.122 --> 18:27.067
No, thanks. You don't need to waste that on me.

18:27.106 --> 18:31.676
Don't say that! It wouldn't be a waste at all.

18:31.970 --> 18:35.934
Well, I guess I'll take you up
on that if I end up needing it.

18:36.247 --> 18:38.247
Sure! The offer stands!

18:38.278 --> 18:39.278
Thanks.

18:39.606 --> 18:43.961
I'm really glad I got a chance
to talk to him today.

18:44.059 --> 18:45.329
Ayanokouji?

18:46.286 --> 18:48.286
May I have a moment, please?

18:50.625 --> 18:52.887
Okay, I'll get going, then!

18:52.965 --> 18:53.629
Okay.

18:53.708 --> 18:54.918
See you later!

18:55.661 --> 19:00.446
Don't you think this additional exam
is a little unreasonable?

19:00.759 --> 19:02.145
Well, yeah.

19:02.243 --> 19:04.625
There's a reason for that.

19:05.212 --> 19:09.645
A few days ago, my father
was suspended as chairman.

19:10.407 --> 19:13.668
I suspect someone may be up to no good.

19:14.118 --> 19:20.856
Perhaps this exam was thrown together hastily
to ensure a particular student is expelled.

19:21.188 --> 19:23.375
It seems possible, does it not?

19:23.552 --> 19:26.290
You're talking about me, I assume.

19:26.403 --> 19:32.946
I would understand the school's intentions in
holding such an odd exam, if that were the case.

19:33.474 --> 19:37.477
So, a certain someone is involved in this.

19:37.927 --> 19:43.157
Accordingly, I'd like to delay
our battle until next time.

19:43.392 --> 19:45.305
Whatever you want to do.

19:45.345 --> 19:46.946
Thank you kindly.

19:47.142 --> 19:50.618
This way, I can put my full focus on Class A.

19:51.360 --> 19:52.727
One more thing…

19:53.313 --> 20:01.313
We have a truce for now, so I won't make
any move against you during this exam.

20:01.536 --> 20:03.821
Are you sure about that?

20:03.958 --> 20:11.282
In the unlikely event that I cause
any negative outcome for you,

20:12.083 --> 20:14.641
I will admit defeat.

20:15.169 --> 20:18.664
I'll let you refuse any further
competitions, as well.

20:19.368 --> 20:26.086
If I get the most negative votes, there
won't be further competitions anyway.

20:26.145 --> 20:28.039
I suppose you're right.

20:28.118 --> 20:33.938
Do you think your underlings will hold off on
betraying you long enough for you to take me on?

20:35.345 --> 20:42.922
How droll. The moment the exam was announced,
I knew exactly who I wanted to have expelled.

20:43.855 --> 20:45.969
Katsuragi Kouhei, of course.

20:46.399 --> 20:48.399
That makes sense.

20:48.841 --> 20:51.536
How will Class C proceed?

20:51.997 --> 20:54.036
I'm not getting involved.

20:54.465 --> 20:55.696
Is that so?

20:56.177 --> 20:59.563
Ryuuen is the easy choice for Class D.

21:00.032 --> 21:02.970
Class B is a bit of a mystery, however.

21:05.286 --> 21:09.200
The best part of the whole exam will be seeing

21:09.701 --> 21:12.551
which dear friend they decide to get rid of.

21:13.468 --> 21:17.413
Well then, I'll see you for our battle
at the end of the year.

21:17.747 --> 21:19.387
Don't forget.

21:19.720 --> 21:20.969
Yeah.

21:35.911 --> 21:37.610
I've been expecting you.

21:37.669 --> 21:39.669
President Nagumo.

21:39.798 --> 21:44.348
So, about those private points…

21:46.595 --> 21:48.595
I, um…

21:52.122 --> 21:54.641
Go out with me, Honami.

21:54.666 --> 21:55.666
Huh?

21:56.713 --> 22:00.697
That's my only condition. Easy, right?

22:05.940 --> 22:09.212
I have to protect my class…
